# Two images build from the repository root — nginx (conf.d + frontend/src) and
# keycloak (the theme + the mark) — so this file is what they are handed. It is
# not the same list as .gitignore: that one is about what a commit carries, this
# one about what the daemon receives.

# --- Feature Start ---
# The certificate is the operator's, mounted at /etc/nginx/certs and never baked
# (INSTALL.md §1). No COPY reaches it, so it was in no layer — but "secrets are
# never in the image" is a weaker rule than "the private key is not handed to
# the build", and the second one is the one worth keeping.
.env
certs/
# --- Feature End ---

# Measured on the nginx build: 2.526 GB of context before this line, 171.6 kB
# after, and almost all of it was one directory no Dockerfile reads.
# `backend/.dockerignore` covers `target/` only for the backend's own build,
# whose context is ./backend — these two start a level up and were shipping
# every Rust artifact on the disk to the daemon. The `**/` is load-bearing: a
# Docker pattern is matched against the whole path, so a bare `target/` misses
# `backend/target/` and the measurement stayed where it was (docs/07).
**/target/
# A cut release: the saved images of the previous one, ~400 MB, never an input.
dist/
.git/

docs/
tmp/
.rules/
.github/
*.md
